<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04Q9">Definition <span data-tag="04Q9">7.6.2.33</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $f: X \rightarrow Y$ be a morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. We will say that a functor $f^{\ast }: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/Y} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/X}$ is <em>given by pullback along $f$</em> if it is a right adjoint to the functor $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/X} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/Y}$ given by postcomposition with $f$ (see Example <a data-tag="04Q4" href="/tag/04Q4">4.3.6.15</a>). Note that this condition characterizes the functor $f^{\ast }$ up to isomorphism (see Remark <a data-tag="02F3" href="/tag/02F3">6.2.1.19</a>). </p>
</article>
